            <div xml:id="d340">

                <pb facs="0429" n="325" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg325"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">733.35/26: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Uruguay (Wright) to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Montevideo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-07-20T18:00:00-03:30">July 20, 1932—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 7:12 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>44. Uruguayan press today carries Department’s announcement to the press
                    regarding extension of our good offices. The delicacy of the situation arising
                    from the change in attitude of the Argentine Government, of which Bliss has kept me closely informed, has
                    rendered it advisable for me to limit my reply to all press inquiries here:
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“I have as yet received no official information that my Government has
                            made such an announcement to the press.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wright</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
